#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cycle, Scheduler and ESS Power"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/architecture.adoc[Edge Architecture] explains the input-process-"
"output model, the Scheduler and the Process Image. This page adds the "
"details from the code. Responsible for the Cycle is the singleton component "
"`+_cycle+` (`+io.openems.edge.core+`, classes `+CycleImpl+` and "
"`+CycleWorker+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cycle time"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-cycle-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Default: **1000 ms** (`+Cycle.DEFAULT_CYCLE_TIME+`), adjustable in the "
"component “Core Cycle” (field `+cycleTime+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-cycle-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"`+_cycle/MeasuredCycleTime+` contains the time actually used by a Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-cycle-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"For troubleshooting, there is a log verbosity (`+CycleLogVerbosity+`): "
"summary, phases or individual components, each with time measurement."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-cycle-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"At the beginning of each Cycle, the operating system's watchdog (systemd) is "
"notified. If the Cycle hangs, systemd can restart the service, provided the "
"watchdog is active in the service file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sequence of a Cycle"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-sequence-of-a-cycle
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"The order is in `+CycleWorker.forever()+`. All Cycle Events are sent "
"synchronously via the Event Admin (`+EdgeEventConstants+`); the next step "
"only starts when all receivers have finished."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| No.\n"
"| Step\n"
"| Typical use\n"
"\n"
"| 1\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_PROCESS_IMAGE+`\n"
"| Drivers hand over read values; Modbus Bridge completes read tasks\n"
"| 2\n"
"| **Switch Process Image**: for each enabled component (except `+_sum+`) `+channel.nextProcessImage()+`\n"
"| from here on `+value()+` returns the new values\n"
"| 3\n"
"| Calculate `+_sum+` (`+updateChannelsBeforeProcessImage()+`) and switch its Process Image\n"
"| totals match the device values just adopted\n"
"| 4\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_AFTER_PROCESS_IMAGE+`\n"
"| Components calculate derived values; with strategy `+BALANCE+`, `+_power+` rebuilds the model here\n"
"| 5\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_CONTROLLERS+`\n"
"| preparations before the Controllers\n"
"| 6\n"
"| **Execute Scheduler and Controllers**\n"
"| `+Controller.run()+` in Scheduler order\n"
"| 7\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_AFTER_CONTROLLERS+`\n"
"| evaluation of the Controller results\n"
"| 8\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_WRITE+`\n"
"| `+_power+` solves the power distribution and calls `+applyPower()+` of the ESS\n"
"| 9\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_EXECUTE_WRITE+`\n"
"| Drivers write setpoints to the devices\n"
"| 10\n"
"| Event `+TOPIC_CYCLE_AFTER_WRITE+`\n"
"| clean-up; `+_power+` (solver v1) discards the constraints of this Cycle\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"An exception anywhere in this sequence only aborts the current Cycle; it is "
"logged as “Error in Scheduler …” (with stack trace for "
"`+NullPointerException+` and `+ClassCastException+`). The next Cycle starts "
"normally."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scheduler and Controllers"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Without a Scheduler, no Controllers run; the log then reports “There are no "
"Schedulers configured!”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Several Schedulers are possible; they run sorted by their Component-ID. Each "
"Scheduler provides an ordered list of Controller IDs via `+getControllers()"
"+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Available Schedulers: `+allalphabetically+` (optionally a fixed list first, "
"then all other Controllers alphabetically by ID), `+fixedorder+` (fixed "
"list), `+daily+` (by time of day), `+jscalendar+` (by calendar rules)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"If a Controller is missing or the ID is not a Controller, the Scheduler sets "
"its State-Channel `+ControllerIsMissing+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"A disabled Controller is skipped; `+_cycle/IgnoreDisabledController+` is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-scheduler-and-controllers
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"If `+run()+` throws an exception, it is logged, the State-Channel "
"`+RunFailed+` (level FAULT) of the Controller is set and the next Controller "
"is executed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meaning of the order"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-meaning-of-the-order
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Controllers that set ESS setpoints work via **constraints** of the power "
"distribution. An earlier Controller can set constraints that later ones must "
"comply with. Example: a Controller for § 14a sets a maximum charging power; "
"a self-consumption Controller running later then receives at most this "
"value. Limiting Controllers therefore come **before** optimizing ones in the "
"order. Details on § 14a are on the user page xref:user/storage-control/"
"section-14a-enwg.adoc[§ 14a]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "ESS Power (`+_power+`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-ess-power-power
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"ESS (`+ManagedSymmetricEss+`) do not have setpoints written directly. "
"Controllers set constraints, and the component `+_power+` (bundle "
"`+io.openems.edge.ess.core+`, “ESS Power”) solves them together for all ESS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting constraints"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Method on the ESS\n"
"| Channel\n"
"| Constraint\n"
"\n"
"| `+setActivePowerEqualsWithFilter(p)+`\n"
"| `+SetActivePowerEquals+`\n"
"| power = p, with control filter\n"
"| `+setActivePowerEqualsWithoutFilter(p)+`\n"
"| `+SetActivePowerEquals+`\n"
"| power = p, without filter\n"
"| `+setActivePowerLessOrEquals(p)+`\n"
"| `+SetActivePowerLessOrEquals+`\n"
"| power ≤ p\n"
"| `+setActivePowerGreaterOrEquals(p)+`\n"
"| `+SetActivePowerGreaterOrEquals+`\n"
"| power ≥ p\n"
"| accordingly `+…ReactivePower…+`\n"
"| \n"
"| reactive power\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Signs: **negative = charge, positive = discharge**. Writing to one of these "
"Channels immediately creates a constraint at the solver via "
"`+onChannelSetNextWrite+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"**With filter** for closed control loops that react to a grid meter (e.g. "
"self-consumption optimization). The filter prevents oscillation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"**Without filter** if the value comes directly from a higher-level "
"Controller or from the user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"For your own constraints, there is `+addPowerConstraint(…)+` or "
"`+addPowerConstraintAndValidate(…)+`; the latter throws an exception if the "
"constraint is incompatible with the previous ones."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"`+getPower().getMaxPower(…)+` and `+getMinPower(…)+` return the leeway that "
"remains after the previous constraints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solving and applying"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-solving-and-applying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Constraints only apply for one Cycle. Solver v1 discards them after writing "
"(step 10) and creates the static limits of the ESS anew "
"(`+getStaticConstraints()+`, e.g. permitted charging/discharging power); "
"solver v2 rebuilds its model after the Process Image is switched (step 4). A "
"Controller must therefore set its setpoints anew in every Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-solving-and-applying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Solving takes place before writing (step 8). Each ESS receives the result "
"via `+applyPower(activePower, reactivePower)+`; the driver converts it into "
"device registers. Rounding is done to `+getPowerPrecision()+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-solving-and-applying
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"If no solution is possible, the State-Channel `+_power/NotSolved+` (level "
"WARNING) is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strategies and filters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Default\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| `+strategy+`\n"
"| `+OPTIMIZE_BY_MOVING_TOWARDS_TARGET+`\n"
"| distribution across several ESS. All strategies except `+BALANCE+` use solver v1 (linear optimization); `+BALANCE+` uses the newer solver v2 (`+TreeSolver+`).\n"
"| `+enablePid+`\n"
"| on\n"
"| PID filter for “with filter” setpoints; parameters `+p+`, `+i+`, `+d+`\n"
"| `+enablePT1Filter+`\n"
"| off\n"
"| PT1 filter instead of PID (only if PID is off), time constant `+pt1TimeConstant+`\n"
"| `+symmetricMode+`\n"
"| on\n"
"| keeps asymmetric ESS symmetric\n"
"| `+debugMode+`\n"
"| off\n"
"| additional log output of the solver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notes for your own code"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-notes-for-your-own-code
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"In `+run()+`, only work with `+value()+`, not with `+getNextValue()+`; "
"otherwise the Controller sees a value that other Controllers do not yet see "
"in the same Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-notes-for-your-own-code
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"A value that a Controller writes to a Channel (`+_setNextValue+`) can only "
"be read via `+value()+` in the next Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-notes-for-your-own-code
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc
msgid ""
"Slow work (network, calculations over many seconds) belongs in a separate "
"thread or worker (`+AbstractWorker+`, `+AbstractCycleWorker+`), not in "
"`+run()+` or a Cycle Event. All events run synchronously and extend the "
"Cycle."
msgstr ""
